  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing life-saving humanitarian protection and health care assistance to migrants and other vulnerable individuals in Lebanon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the project is to improve access to life-saving protection and health-care services for migrants in Lebanon. The project continues IOM&#x2019;s efforts to mitigate the impact of socioeconomic and humanitarian crises on the protection environment for migrants, including but not limited to unaccompanied and separated children and victims of human trafficking. The project targets 600 affected people with Health engagements, 2,510 with Protection and 530 with Protection-CP activities.</narrative>
  </description>
